#!/usr/bin/python3
"""hearth-home-server: Mantel's Settings › Home server (docs/HOME-SERVER.md). This PC as a home server for your other
devices: shared folders (Samba), drives and snapshots, Tailscale. Builds on Hearth Storage (Hearth Link's home server
for Hearth devices); the root half is /usr/libexec/nimbus/hearth-home-server-helper (through pkexec).

Your choices live in ~/.config/nimbus/home-server.json, written only when you change something, through
hearth_settings_io (atomic, .bak, merge under a lock; defaults are filled in when it's read, never saved). The
system's config (Samba's, the firewall's, the snapshot timer's) is made from it by the root helper, which checks
everything again.

  hearth-home-server status                     JSON: your settings (with defaults), the shares and whether each can
                                                take snapshots, what's installed, Tailscale in short, hidden items
  hearth-home-server set KEY VALUE              lightMode, tsOnly, tsBoot, exitNode, taildropReceive, wakeFromAway,
                                                snapshots, showHidden, setupDone (on|off); ccDays (1-365);
                                                keepHourly, keepDaily, keepWeekly (numbers)
  hearth-home-server candidates                 folders you might share (Home's folders, drives' folders)
  hearth-home-server pick-folder                Hearth Files' folder picker; prints the folder
  hearth-home-server share-add PATH [NAME]      share a folder (read only, home network, recycle bin on)
  hearth-home-server share-set ID KEY VALUE     on|write|recycle|snapshots on|off; reach home|tailscale; name NAME
  hearth-home-server share-remove ID            stop sharing it (its files are never touched)
  hearth-home-server smb-password               your sharing password on stdin (HEARTH_INPUT); never kept
  hearth-home-server apply                      make the system match your settings again
  hearth-home-server drives                     every drive's space, health and temperature
  hearth-home-server format-plan DEV            what formatting a drive would do, and what to confirm
  hearth-home-server format                     JSON on stdin (see hearth-home-server-helper)
  hearth-home-server snapshots ID               a share's snapshots (newest first)
  hearth-home-server restore ID SNAPSHOT        copy the share as it was into a new folder in Home (never over it)
  hearth-home-server ts-status | ts-start | ts-login | ts-logout | ts-ping
  hearth-home-server ts-send PEER [FILE]        Taildrop: send a file (picked in Hearth Files when not given)
  hearth-home-server seen KIND                  note that KIND (commandCenter, camera, ups) was seen just now
  ---- stage 2
  hearth-home-server set KEY VALUE              also: alertsOn, alertSmart, alertFull, alertBackup, alertMirror,
                                                alertTailscale, keepAwake, schedule, ups, receiveOn (on|off);
                                                alertFullPct (80|85|90|95); sleepIdle (0|30|60|120|240 minutes);
                                                spinDown (0|10|20|30|60 minutes); sleepAt, wakeAt (HH:MM)
  hearth-home-server person-add NAME            a person (Samba only, no login); their password on stdin (HEARTH_INPUT)
  hearth-home-server person-password NAME       their new password on stdin
  hearth-home-server person-remove NAME         they can't open anything anymore; their files stay
  hearth-home-server person-access NAME ID none|read|write
  hearth-home-server person-folder NAME on [BASE]|off    their own folder (Home › People › NAME, or BASE/People/NAME)
  hearth-home-server person-quota NAME GB       a limit for their own folder (btrfs only; 0 for none)
  hearth-home-server backup-add                 JSON on stdin {name, shares, target, every, at, password, code, cloud}
  hearth-home-server backup-set ID KEY VALUE    on (on|off), every, at, day, name, keepDaily, keepWeekly, keepMonthly
  hearth-home-server backup-share ID SHARE on|off
  hearth-home-server backup-password ID         its new password on stdin
  hearth-home-server backup-remove ID           the job goes (its password and keys too); the backup itself stays
  hearth-home-server backup-now ID | backup-snapshots ID | backup-restore ID SNAPSHOT PATH | backup-targets
  hearth-home-server receive-path PATH | receive-add NAME | receive-remove USER     backups from your other Hearth devices
  hearth-home-server sync-status | sync-id | sync-add PATH PEER DEVICEID | sync-accept FOLDER DEVICE [PATH] | sync-remove ID
  hearth-home-server alerts-test | alert-peer NAME on|off | ups-status
  hearth-home-server quick                      Home server in short, for Game Mode's Quick Access
  hearth-home-server quick-set lightMode on|off saved only (from Game Mode, where no password can be asked)
  hearth-home-server resume on|off              let jobs paused for your game run now (up to 4 hours), or pause them again
Output: one JSON line; failures print "error: ..." and exit 1.
"""
